acchi</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Quetiapine may induce mania:a case report</article-title><source>Can J Psychiatry</source><volume>48</volume><fpage>349</fpage><lpage>350</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12866345</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b12-ndt-2-139"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Borison</surname><given-names>RL</given-names></name><name><surname>Arvanitis</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name><name><surname>Miller</surname><given-names>BG</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>ICI 204, 636, an atypical antipsychotic:efficacy and safety in a multicenter, placebo-controlled trial in patients with schizophrenia. US SEROQUEL Study Group</article-title><source>J Clin Psychopharmacol</source><volume>16</volume><fpage>158</fpage><lpage>69</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8690831</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b13-ndt-2-139"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bourin</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Lambert</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Guitton</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Treatment of acute mania from clinical trials to recommendations for clinical practice</article-title><source>Hum Psychopharmacol</source><volume>20</volume><fpage>15</fpage><lpage>26</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15568205</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b14-ndt-2-139"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bowden</surname><given-names>CL</given-names></name><name><surname>Grunze</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Mullen</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>A randomized, double- blind, placebo-controlled efficacy and s